---
/* DRAFT - must be reviewed by a licensed US attorney before publishing. */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, addressLines } from '../config/site';

const { legal } = site;

const toc = [
	{ id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are and scope of this policy' },
	{ id: 'information-we-collect', title: 'Information we collect' },
	{ id: 'how-we-use-information', title: 'How we use information' },
	{ id: 'analytics-and-cookies', title: 'Analytics and cookies' },
	{ id: 'third-party-processors', title: 'Third-party processors' },
	{ id: 'retention', title: 'Data retention' },
	{ id: 'security', title: 'Data security' },
	{ id: 'childrens-privacy', title: "Children's privacy (COPPA)" },
	{ id: 'california-rights', title: 'California rights (CCPA/CPRA)' },
	{ id: 'other-state-laws', title: 'Other US state privacy laws' },
	{ id: 'email-communications', title: 'Email communications (CAN-SPAM)' },
	{ id: 'policy-changes', title: 'Policy changes' },
	{ id: 'contact', title: 'How to contact us' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	intro="This policy explains what information Linkly LLC collects through this website, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We have written it in plain language rather than boilerplate."
	lastUpdated={legal.effectiveDate}
	toc={toc}
	seo={{
		title: 'Privacy Policy',
		description:
			'How Linkly LLC collects, uses, retains and protects personal information from this website, including CCPA/CPRA, COPPA and other US state privacy rights.',
	}}
>
	<h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are and scope of this policy</h2>
	<p>
		{legal.entityName} ("{site.name}", "we", "us") is a business organised in
		the state of
		{legal.stateOfFormation}. This Privacy Policy applies to this website and to
		the project inquiry form on it. It does not apply to any other website we
		link to, and it does not cover personal information we handle solely on
		behalf of a client under a signed agreement — that is governed by the
		client's own policy and our agreement with them.
	</p>

	<h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>
	<p>
		We collect four kinds of information. You can read this section as the short
		version: we collect what you type into our form, what your browser sends
		automatically, and nothing else.
	</p>

	<h3>Information you give us</h3>
	<p>
		When you submit the project inquiry form, we collect the name, email
		address, project type, budget range and message you enter. We use this only
		to respond to your inquiry. The form also records a timestamp of when the
		page was rendered so we can reject automated submissions.
	</p>

	<h3>Information from your use of the site</h3>
	<p>
		Like every web server, ours records standard request logs. These include
		your IP address, the URL and page you requested, the date and time, the
		referring page, your browser's user-agent string, and the HTTP status
		returned. We use these to keep the site running, to investigate errors, and
		to detect abuse.
	</p>

	<h3>Cookies set by us</h3>
	<p>
		We set one piece of browser storage that is not a cookie and never leaves
		your browser: your light or dark theme preference. It cannot be used to
		identify you and is not transmitted to us. It is stored under the key <code
			>theme</code
		> in your browser's local storage.
	</p>

	<h3>Analytics</h3>
	<p>
		If, and only if, privacy-friendly analytics is enabled on this site, the
		provider below receives a record of page views. The provider is cookie-free:
		it does not set cookies, does not build a persistent profile of you across
		websites, and does not collect your IP address for storage. You can review
		and change your choices at any time on our <a href="/cookie-preferences"
			>cookie preferences</a
		> page.
	</p>

	<h2 id="how-we-use-information">How we use information</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>To respond to you.</strong> We use your form submission to answer your
			inquiry and, if we work together, to prepare and deliver a project.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>To run and secure the site.</strong> Server logs are used for troubleshooting,
			capacity planning, rate limiting and abuse prevention.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>To comply with law.</strong> We retain and disclose information when
			we are legally required to.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>To understand aggregate usage.</strong> Where analytics is enabled,
			we look at aggregate page-view counts. We do not use it to profile individual
			visitors.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not sell your personal information. We do not share it for
		cross-context behavioural advertising. We do not use it for automated
		decision-making that has a legal or similarly significant effect on you.
	</p>

	<h2 id="analytics-and-cookies">Analytics and cookies</h2>
	<p>
		This site does not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, session
		recorders, or fingerprinting. If analytics is enabled it is provided by
		Plausible Analytics, which is designed around the GDPR and CCPA's opt-out
		model: no cookies, no cross-site tracking, and no personal data is
		collected. Because no personal data is collected, a consent banner is not
		required before analytics loads.
	</p>
	<p>
		If that changes in future — for example if a third-party tool is added that
		does set cookies — we will update this policy first, add a consent banner,
		and make sure nothing loads before you consent. Your
		<a href="/cookie-preferences">cookie preferences</a> page is the single place
		to check what is currently active and to turn it off.
	</p>
	<p>
		Your browser also sends a <code>Do Not Track</code> header if you have enabled
		Do Not Track. Because we do not track you across websites, we honour that signal
		by loading nothing beyond what the page needs to display. We do not respond to
		Global Privacy Control differently, because we do not sell or share personal information
		and there is nothing to opt out of.
	</p>

	<h2 id="third-party-processors">Third-party processors</h2>
	<p>
		We use a small number of vendors to operate the site. They act as processors
		on our instructions and are not permitted to use your information for their
		own purposes.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Email delivery — Resend.</strong> When you submit the contact form,
			the details you entered are sent through Resend to deliver the notification
			email to us. Message content and your email address are processed for delivery
			and then discarded on Resend's infrastructure.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Analytics — Plausible Analytics,</strong> only if enabled. Receives
			aggregate page-view data with no cookies, as described above.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Hosting and CDN — Vercel.</strong> Serves the site, processes request
			data, and runs the form submission endpoint. Request logs include your IP address.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong
				>Domain and email hosting — [PLACEHOLDER: email/domain provider].</strong
			> [PLACEHOLDER: state who registers and hosts the domain and mailboxes for Linkly
			LLC]
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Typefaces and icons — Google Fonts and Iconify.</strong> Our stylesheet
			requests font files from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address in the
			ordinary course of serving them. Icon artwork is bundled at build time and is
			not fetched at runtime.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not add advertising or social tracking pixels to this site. If that
		changes, this list and the <a href="/cookie-preferences"
			>cookie preferences</a
		> page will change with it.
	</p>

	<h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
	<p>We keep information only as long as we have a reason to.</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Contact form submissions.</strong> Kept for as long as needed to manage
			the resulting business relationship, and afterwards only as needed to satisfy
			legal, tax or accounting record-keeping obligations.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Server logs.</strong> Retained for a short operational period and then
			deleted or aggregated. [PLACEHOLDER: state the actual log retention period,
			e.g. "30 days"]
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Analytics data.</strong> Held in aggregate by the analytics provider
			and not tied to an individual.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Theme preference.</strong> Stays in your browser's local storage until
			you clear it. We never receive it.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Client project data.</strong> Handled under the terms of the governing
			agreement, which sets its own retention schedule.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="security">Data security</h2>
	<p>
		We use encryption in transit (HTTPS/TLS) for all pages and for form
		submissions. The contact endpoint validates and sanitises every field
		server-side, applies rate limiting and spam filtering, and never logs full
		message contents. Administrative access to production is limited to the
		people who need it.
	</p>
	<p>
		No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal information
		and is likely to cause you harm, we will notify you and the relevant
		regulator as required by applicable law.
	</p>

	<h2 id="childrens-privacy">Children's privacy (COPPA)</h2>
	<p>
		This site is a business-to-business website. It is not directed to children
		under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children
		under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 16 for
		the purpose of marketing. If you believe a child has submitted information
		through our form, contact us at the address below and we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2 id="california-rights">California rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
	<p>
		If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act as
		amended by the California Privacy Rights Act gives you rights over your
		personal information. This section describes those rights and how to
		exercise them.
	</p>

	<h3>Categories of personal information we collect</h3>
	<p>
		In the twelve months preceding this policy's effective date we have
		collected the following categories: <strong>(A) Identifiers</strong> — name and
		email address, from the contact form; <strong
			>(B) Internet or other electronic network activity</strong
		> — server log data such as IP address, browser type, referring page and pages
		viewed; and <strong>(C) Geolocation data</strong> — derived from an IP address
		at a coarse precision and used only to determine the appropriate time zone for
		a response.
	</p>

	<h3>Sources of that information</h3>
	<p>
		Directly from you when you use the contact form, and automatically from your
		browser when you visit any page.
	</p>

	<h3>Purposes of use and categories of sources</h3>
	<p>
		Business and commercial purposes listed in the "How we use information"
		section above, and for security and legal compliance.
	</p>

	<h3>Rights you have</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to know.</strong> You may ask us to disclose the categories and
			specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you, the sources,
			the purposes, and the categories of third parties we disclosed it to.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to delete.</strong> You may ask us to delete personal information
			we have collected from you, subject to certain exceptions.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to correct.</strong> You may ask us to correct inaccurate personal
			information.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to opt out of sale or sharing.</strong> We do not sell personal
			information and do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising, so
			there is nothing to opt out of. We do not sell or share the personal information
			of anyone under 16.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to limit use of sensitive personal information.</strong> We do
			not collect sensitive personal information as defined by the CPRA, so we do
			not use or disclose it for the purpose of inferring characteristics about you.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Right to non-discrimination.</strong> We will not deny you services,
			charge a different price, or provide a different level or quality of service
			because you exercised a right under the CCPA/CPRA.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>How to submit a request</h3>
	<p>
		Send an email to {legal.contactEmail} with the subject line "California privacy
		request", or write to us at the postal address in the contact section. Please
		describe what you want and include enough detail for us to locate the relevant
		information. We will confirm receipt within 10 business days and respond substantively
		within 45 calendar days. If we need more time, we will tell you and why. We may
		verify your identity before fulfilling the request by asking for information we
		already hold about you. We do not charge a fee unless the request is manifestly
		unfounded, excessive or repetitive.
	</p>

	<h3>Shine the Light (CalOPPA) disclosures</h3>
	<p>
		California residents may request disclosure of the categories of personal
		information we disclose to third parties for their own direct marketing
		purposes. We do not disclose personal information to third parties for their
		own direct marketing purposes, so there is nothing to disclose. California
		residents may also opt out of the "sale of personal information" under the
		California Delete Act, which extends "sale" to include any exchange for
		valuable consideration. We do not make such an exchange. [PLACEHOLDER:
		attorney to confirm the current CalOPPA and Delete Act position once
		analytics and any pixel providers are finalised]
	</p>

	<h2 id="other-state-laws">Other US state privacy laws</h2>
	<p>
		Other states have enacted privacy laws that give residents similar rights.
		These include the Virginia Consumer Data Protection Act, the Colorado
		Privacy Act, the Connecticut Data Privacy Act, the Texas Data Privacy and
		Security Act, the Utah Consumer Privacy Act, the Oregon Consumer Privacy
		Act, the Montana Consumer Data Privacy Act, the Delaware Personal Data
		Privacy Act, the Iowa Consumer Data Protection Act, the Indiana Consumer
		Data Protection Act, the Tennessee Information Protection Act, and the New
		Jersey Data Privacy Act.
	</p>
	<p>
		Where those laws apply to you, you have the right to confirm whether we
		process your personal information, to access it, to correct it, to delete
		it, to obtain a portable copy, to opt out of targeted advertising, to opt
		out of the sale of personal information, to limit certain processing, and to
		be free of discrimination for exercising these rights. These rights largely
		mirror the California rights described above.
	</p>
	<p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us as described below.</p>

	<h3>Right to appeal</h3>
	<p>
		If you are a resident of a state whose law provides a right to appeal, and
		we deny your request, you may appeal by replying to our response or writing
		to
		{legal.contactEmail} with the subject line "Privacy appeal". We will acknowledge
		the appeal and respond within the period the applicable law requires — typically
		60 calendar days, extendable by 45 days where the law allows it. If the appeal
		is denied, you may contact your state attorney general to pursue the matter further.
	</p>

	<h2 id="email-communications">Email communications (CAN-SPAM)</h2>
	<p>
		We send commercial email only to people who have asked us to contact them
		about a project. We do not purchase mailing lists, and we do not send
		unsolicited commercial mail. Every commercial email we send complies with
		the CAN-SPAM Act: it identifies us as the sender, provides a valid physical
		postal address, and includes a working unsubscribe mechanism.
	</p>
	<p>
		To stop receiving email from us, use the unsubscribe link in any message, or
		contact us at the address below. Opting out does not affect transactional
		messages about an active project.
	</p>

	<h2 id="policy-changes">Policy changes</h2>
	<p>
		We will update this policy when our practices change. The "Last updated"
		date at the top of this page always reflects the current version. For
		material changes — new processors, new data collected, or a change in how we
		use data — we will post a notice on this site and, for material changes
		affecting people who have contacted us, we will email those people before
		the change takes effect. [PLACEHOLDER: confirm how far in advance notice
		will be given, e.g. "at least 14 days"]
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact">How to contact us</h2>
	<p>
		{legal.entityName}<br />
		{
			addressLines.map(line => (
				<>
					{line}
					<br />
				</>
			))
		}
		Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a>
	</p>
	<p>
		For privacy requests, use the subject line "Privacy request" (or "California
		privacy request" or "Privacy appeal" as appropriate) so it reaches the right
		person without being redirected.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
